-{"id":"cex-a-continuous-image-of-a-locally-compact-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=b49ec80d24320c11a1364c9f100fcf5631b20a73&repid=rep1&type=pdf","https://www.math.toronto.edu/ivan/mat327/docs/notes/19-compactifications.pdf"],"rationale":"The open textbook gives the standard quotient R/Z obtained by collapsing all integers to one point and states that it is not locally compact because every neighbourhood of the collapsed point contains an infinite closed discrete subspace; the university notes also record failure of local compactness under continuous images. The item replaces Z by the embedded naturals and expands the same closed-discrete proof, so it is a semantic and proof-level adaptation. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
+{"id":"cex-a-continuous-image-of-a-locally-compact-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=b49ec80d24320c11a1364c9f100fcf5631b20a73&repid=rep1&type=pdf","https://www.math.toronto.edu/ivan/mat327/docs/notes/19-compactifications.pdf"],"rationale":"The open textbook gives the standard quotient R/Z obtained by collapsing all integers to one point and states that it is not locally compact because every neighbourhood of the collapsed point contains an infinite closed discrete subspace; the university notes also record failure of local compactness under continuous images. The item replaces Z by the embedded naturals and expands the same closed-discrete proof, so it is a semantic and proof-level adaptation. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200); the previously unverified CiteseerX PDF was re-opened successfully through that route at A4 on 2026-08-04.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
