      {
        "fact": "L7",
        "source": "def-topology-basis-subbasis",
        "source_section": "Definition",
        "quote": "Let $(X, \\mathcal{T})$ be a topological space ([[def-topological-space]]).\n\nA family $\\mathcal{B} \\subseteq \\mathcal{T}$ is a **basis for $\\mathcal{T}$** if\nevery open set is a union of members of $\\mathcal{B}$: for every\n$U \\in \\mathcal{T}$ there is $\\mathcal{B}_U \\subseteq \\mathcal{B}$ with\n$U = \\bigcup \\mathcal{B}_U$. Equivalently, and this is the form used in proofs,\n\n$$\\text{for every } U \\in \\mathcal{T} \\text{ and every } x \\in U \\text{ there is } B \\in \\mathcal{B} \\text{ with } x \\in B \\subseteq U .$$",
        "uses": [
          "4.2"
