        "fact": "L3",
        "source": "lem-sup-epsilon",
        "source_section": "Statement",
        "quote": "Let $S \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ be nonempty and bounded above, and let $u$ be an\nupper bound of $S$ ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]). Then\n\n$$u = \\sup S \\quad \\Longleftrightarrow \\quad \\text{for every } \\varepsilon > 0 \\text{ there exists } s \\in S \\text{ with } u - \\varepsilon < s.$$",
        "uses": [
